[]{#subsection:filtration label="subsection:filtration"}

#### The filtration and the associated graded module.

The module $M$ is said to be pure isoclinic of slope $\mu$ if $S(M) = \{\mu\}$ and fuchsian if moreover $\mu = 0$. Direct sums of pure isoclinic modules are called pure modules [^1]: they are irregular objects without wild monodromy, as follows from [@RSZ] and [@JSSTO]. The tannakian subcategory of ${\mathcal{E}}^{(0)}$ made up of pure modules is called ${\mathcal{E}}^{(0)}_{p}$. Modules with integral slopes also form tannakian subcategories, which we write ${\mathcal{E}}^{(0)}_{1}$

